1
00:00:06,430 --> 00:00:09,110
Four swimmers finish a race.

2
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:17,380
Their times are 58.4 seconds, 58.39 seconds, 58.04 seconds, and 58.415 seconds.

3
00:00:17,430 --> 00:00:18,980
The smallest time wins.

4
00:00:19,030 --> 00:00:20,030
Which time won?

5
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:23,310
Pause the video and decide.

6
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:27,410
Every time starts with 58, so look at the tenths.

7
00:00:27,460 --> 00:00:29,000
58.04 has 0 tenths.

8
00:00:29,050 --> 00:00:32,050
The others have 3 or 4 tenths.

9
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:35,250
So 58.04 seconds is the smallest time.

10
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:37,230
That swimmer won.

11
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:38,720
Remember these signs.

12
00:00:38,770 --> 00:00:41,240
Less than, and greater than.

13
00:00:41,290 --> 00:00:43,820
Equal to, and not equal to.

14
00:00:43,870 --> 00:00:45,510
0.5 is equal to 0.50.

15
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:50,670
A zero at the end of a decimal does not change its value.

16
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:54,450
To compare decimals, start with the whole-number parts.

17
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:57,810
If they are the same, compare the tenths.

18
00:00:57,860 --> 00:01:00,010
Compare 58.4 and 58.39.

19
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:02,310
The whole numbers match.

20
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:04,510
The tenths are 4 and 3.

21
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:09,170
4 is bigger, so 58.4 is greater than 58.39.

22
00:01:09,220 --> 00:01:14,040
You only move on to the hundredths when the tenths are the same.

23
00:01:14,090 --> 00:01:15,600
Here is a useful trick.

24
00:01:15,650 --> 00:01:21,800
Write zeros at the end, so that every number has the same number of decimal places.

25
00:01:21,850 --> 00:01:28,400
Now compare them like whole numbers: 400, 390, 40 and 415.

26
00:01:28,450 --> 00:01:35,500
In order, smallest first: 58.04, 58.39, 58.4, 58.415.

27
00:01:35,550 --> 00:01:36,460
Be careful.

28
00:01:36,510 --> 00:01:39,690
A longer number is not always bigger.

29
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:42,590
0.7 is greater than 0.6999.

30
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:43,280
Your turn.

31
00:01:43,330 --> 00:01:45,920
Which of these numbers is the largest?

32
00:01:45,970 --> 00:01:49,200
Pause the video and choose.

33
00:01:49,250 --> 00:01:50,520
The answer is 0.6.

34
00:01:50,570 --> 00:01:51,690
It has 6 tenths.

35
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:57,440
The other numbers have fewer tenths, even though they have more digits.

36
00:01:57,490 --> 00:01:58,790
Here is the method.

37
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:02,810
Step 1: line the numbers up by the decimal point.

38
00:02:02,860 --> 00:02:09,560
Step 2: fill empty places with zeros, so they all have the same number of decimal places.

39
00:02:09,610 --> 00:02:15,790
Step 3: compare the whole numbers, then the tenths, then the hundredths, and so on.

40
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:19,520
Step 4: write the original numbers in order.

41
00:02:19,570 --> 00:02:26,550
Write these in order, smallest first: 6.2, 6.05, 6.199 and 6.21.

42
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:29,400
Give them all 3 decimal places.

43
00:02:29,450 --> 00:02:32,880
Compare 200, 50, 199 and 210.

44
00:02:32,930 --> 00:02:39,310
The smallest is 50, then 199, then 200, then 210.

45
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:44,710
So the order is 6.05, 6.199, 6.2, 6.21.

46
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:49,560
Which is smaller: negative 1.4, or negative 1.35?

47
00:02:49,610 --> 00:02:54,550
Without the signs, 1.40 is bigger than 1.35.

48
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:57,160
So negative 1.4 is further from zero.

49
00:02:57,210 --> 00:03:02,080
It is further left on the number line, which makes it smaller.

50
00:03:02,130 --> 00:03:06,270
Negative 1.4 is less than negative 1.35.

51
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:07,080
Your turn.

52
00:03:07,130 --> 00:03:11,070
Which is smaller: negative 0.3, or negative 0.25?

53
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:13,860
Pause and decide.

54
00:03:13,910 --> 00:03:16,070
0.30 is bigger than 0.25.

55
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:22,560
So negative 0.3 is further from zero, and it is the smaller number.

56
00:03:22,610 --> 00:03:24,750
Is 4.30 equal to 4.3?

57
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:25,170
Yes.

58
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:28,820
4.30 has 3 tenths and 0 hundredths.

59
00:03:28,870 --> 00:03:31,870
That is the same as 4.3.

60
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,950
Is 0.09 equal to 0.9?

61
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:34,240
No.

62
00:03:34,290 --> 00:03:38,940
0.09 is 9 hundredths, but 0.9 is 9 tenths.

63
00:03:38,990 --> 00:03:43,730
Ivy puts 0.8, 0.75 and 0.125 in order, smallest first.

64
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:46,760
Which line goes wrong first?

65
00:03:46,810 --> 00:03:47,950
Line 1 is wrong.

66
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,510
The number of digits does not tell you the size.

67
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:54,350
Compare the tenths: 8, 7 and 1.

68
00:03:54,400 --> 00:04:00,270
The correct order, smallest first, is 0.125, 0.75, 0.8.

69
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:04,360
Ordering decimals decides who gets the gold medal.

70
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:12,110
At the 2008 Olympic Games, Michael Phelps won the 100 metres butterfly in 50.58 seconds.

71
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:16,740
The swimmer in second place took 50.59 seconds.

72
00:04:16,790 --> 00:04:18,390
The tenths are the same.

73
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:20,730
Only the hundredths are different.

74
00:04:20,780 --> 00:04:24,100
He won by just one hundredth of a second!

75
00:04:24,150 --> 00:04:25,770
One last question.

76
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:30,120
How many of these numbers are greater than 1.1?

77
00:04:30,170 --> 00:04:32,630
1.5, 1.05, 1.505 and 1.055.

78
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:36,440
Pause the video and count.

79
00:04:36,490 --> 00:04:38,990
Compare the tenths with 1.1.

80
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:43,460
1.5 and 1.505 have 5 tenths, so they are greater.

81
00:04:43,510 --> 00:04:48,010
1.05 and 1.055 have 0 tenths, so they are smaller.

82
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:50,020
The answer is 2.

83
00:04:50,070 --> 00:04:56,460
To remember: compare the whole numbers, then the tenths, then the hundredths, in turn.

84
00:04:56,510 --> 00:05:02,050
Add zeros at the end, so the numbers have the same number of decimal places.

85
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:04,890
More digits does not mean bigger.

86
00:05:04,940 --> 00:05:09,510
With negative numbers, the one further from zero is smaller.

87
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:14,710
Great work! Now practise lesson 4.1 on Camday.
